{"seq":9,"slug":"environmental-toxicology","title":"环境毒理学","stage":"DONE","category":"environmental-science","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"环境毒理学\">环境毒理学</h1><p>环境毒理学研究的是污染物如何进入环境、又如何作用于生物与人，最终怎样把这种作用转化为可量化、可管理的风险。它不是单纯的「研究毒物」，而是一条从分子机制贯穿到全球公约的完整逻辑链——一个污染物分子从排放口出发，到它在某个人或某只北极熊体内造成损伤、再到监管者据此设限，中间的每一步都是这门学科要回答的问题。</p>\n<p>本 hub 按这条逻辑链分四章递进，环环相扣。</p>\n<p>第一章「毒理学基础」奠定通用语言。先讲剂量-反应关系，把「是否有毒」转化为可建模的定量问题，这是整个学科的基石；再讲吸收分布代谢排泄（ADME），解释外暴露剂量如何变成真正作用于靶器官的内剂量；最后讲毒性作用机制，从分子层面回答「到达靶点后究竟发生了什么」，并引入串联全书的不良结局通路（AOP）框架。</p>\n<p>第二章「环境污染物」把通用原理落到具体对象。持久性有机污染物（POPs）展示「持久、蓄积、迁移、毒性」如何造就全球性威胁；重金属与类金属说明不可降解的元素污染如何靠「形态」决定命运；新兴污染物与微塑料则呈现当代最不确定、监管最滞后的前沿，如 PFAS 与微塑料。</p>\n<p>第三章「环境归趋与暴露」追踪污染物在真实世界里的轨迹。环境迁移与转化讲它在大气、水、土壤、生物之间如何分配、降解；生物富集与放大讲它如何沿食物链层层浓缩，使顶级掠食者最危险；暴露评估则把这些浓度翻译成「某个具体受体实际接触并吸收了多少」。</p>\n<p>第四章「风险评估与管理」是全书的收口。生态风险评估保护种群与生态系统，人体健康风险用四步法保护具体的人尤其脆弱人群，毒理学测试与法规则回答「这些数字从哪来、又如何变成制度约束」。</p>\n<p>四章之间不是孤立模块：基础章提供的剂量-反应基准与机制语言，被污染物章用来解释各类物质的危害，被归趋暴露章用来追踪其行为，最终在风险章汇聚成可供决策的结论。建议初学者按章顺序通读，已有基础者可循文中的交叉链接，沿任一污染物或任一机制纵向贯通全 hub。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"毒理学基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"dose-response","title":"剂量-反应关系","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations/dose-response"},{"seq":2,"slug":"adme","title":"吸收分布代谢排泄","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations/adme"},{"seq":3,"slug":"toxicity-mechanisms","title":"毒性作用机制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations/toxicity-mechanisms"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"pollutants","title":"环境污染物","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/pollutants","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"persistent-organic","title":"持久性有机污染物","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/pollutants/persistent-organic"},{"seq":2,"slug":"heavy-metals","title":"重金属与类金属","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/pollutants/heavy-metals"},{"seq":3,"slug":"emerging-microplastics","title":"新兴污染物与微塑料","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/pollutants/emerging-microplastics"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"fate-exposure","title":"环境归趋与暴露","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"transport-transformation","title":"环境迁移与转化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure/transport-transformation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"bioaccumulation","title":"生物富集与放大","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure/bioaccumulation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"exposure-assessment","title":"暴露评估","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure/exposure-assessment"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"risk","title":"风险评估与管理","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/risk","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"ecological-risk","title":"生态风险评估","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/risk/ecological-risk"},{"seq":2,"slug":"human-health-risk","title":"人体健康风险","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/risk/human-health-risk"},{"seq":3,"slug":"testing-regulation","title":"毒理学测试与法规","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/risk/testing-regulation"}]}]}